-- title:
--   Relaxed Energy Bounded By The Closed-Operator Energy
-- statement:
--   This theorem gives the upper bound for the sequential relaxation of a closable partial linear operator.
--
--   Let $X$ be a real normed space, let $H$ be a real inner-product space, and let $T:X\dashrightarrow H$ be closable. For every $x$ in the domain of the closure $\overline T$, the sequential relaxation of the pre-energy generated by $T$ satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{sequentialRelaxation}_{T}(x)
--   \le
--   \|\overline T x\|_{+}^{\,2}.
--   $$
--
--   Here $\|\cdot\|_{+}$ denotes the nonnegative norm represented by `NNReal`, and the right-hand side is coerced to `ENNReal`. The declaration is `sequentialRelaxation_ofLinearPMap_le`; completeness of the Hilbert target is not required in the declaration's explicit type.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Energy/Relaxation/LinearPMap.lean#L296-L314 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.Relaxation.LinearPMap`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.PreEnergy.sequentialRelaxation_ofLinearPMap_le`; the repository is private at upload time).

